Source: task-ai-desktop
Section: tasks
Priority: optional
Maintainer: AI Workspace Lab <ai-workspace-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/ai-workspace-lab/ai-desktop

Package: task-ai-desktop-core
Architecture: all
Depends:
 dbus-x11,
 xdg-utils,
 xdg-user-dirs,
 x11-utils,
 x11-xserver-utils,
 xauth,
 ca-certificates,
 fontconfig,
 fonts-noto-core,
 fonts-noto-cjk,
 fonts-noto-color-emoji,
 hicolor-icon-theme,
 adwaita-icon-theme,
 gvfs,
 gvfs-backends,
 xfce4-terminal,
 thunar,
 thunar-volman,
 libqt6core6,
 libqt6gui6,
 libqt6qml6,
 libqt6quick6,
 libqt6quickcontrols2-6,
 libqt6widgets6,
 libqt6dbus6,
 qt6-qpa-plugins,
 libxcb1,
 libx11-xcb1,
 xlaunch,
 chromium | firefox-esr,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xorg
Description: core runtime for the AI Workspace desktop
 Common fonts, X11 utilities, Qt runtime, XLaunch, terminal, file manager,
 browser, GVFS, and shared session scripts. This package does not select a
 display manager or window manager.

Package: task-ai-desktop-kde-plasma-core
Architecture: all
Depends:
 task-ai-desktop-core,
 kde-plasma-desktop,
 plasma-workspace,
 kwin-x11,
 kde-cli-tools,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: dolphin, konsole
Suggests: xdock, lightdm, sddm
Description: KDE Plasma core profile for the AI Workspace desktop
 Daily-use KDE Plasma desktop core using XLaunch as the AI application menu.
 XDock remains optional and can be installed when a bottom dock is desired.
 The display manager is selected by the desktop or ISO profile.

Package: task-ai-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends:
 task-ai-desktop-core,
 icewm,
 xdock,
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xorg
Description: ICEWM compatibility profile for task-ai-desktop
 Compatibility meta-package for the original ICEWM desktop profile. It adds
 ICEWM and XDock on top of task-ai-desktop-core.

Package: task-ai-desktop-vps
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, icewm, xvfb, x11vnc, dbus-x11, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: novnc, websockify, xdock
Description: VPS profile for task-ai-desktop
 Adds Xvfb and X11VNC for a headless ICEWM AI desktop without a display
 manager, physical display, or GPU.

Package: task-ai-desktop-container
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, icewm, xvfb, x11vnc, dbus-x11, tini, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: novnc, websockify, xdock
Description: container profile for task-ai-desktop
 Adds Xvfb, X11VNC, D-Bus, and init setup for an OCI container without
 systemd or a display manager. noVNC and websockify provide optional browser
 access.

Package: task-ai-desktop-session
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, icewm, ${misc:Depends}
Description: optional ICEWM session alias for task-ai-desktop
 Selects ICEWM while common session scripts remain owned by the core package.

Package: task-ai-desktop-xdock
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, xdock, ${misc:Depends}
Description: optional XDock integration alias for task-ai-desktop
 Provides the /opt/task-ai-desktop/bin/xdock compatibility path without
 selecting a window manager or display manager.

Package: task-ai-desktop-xlaunch
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, ${misc:Depends}
Description: optional XLaunch integration alias for task-ai-desktop
 Provides the xlaunch and XLaunch compatibility paths; XLaunch is in core.

Package: task-ai-desktop-apps
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, ${misc:Depends}
Description: compatibility alias for shared desktop applications
 The terminal, file manager and browser remain in the shared core profile.

Package: task-ai-desktop-dev
Architecture: all
Depends: task-ai-desktop-core, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: git, gh, python3, golang, nodejs, npm, jq
Description: optional desktop development-tool recommendations
 Keeps development tools out of the mandatory desktop runtime dependencies.
